{"acceptance":["task_declared_event_exists","dispatch_carries_task_and_milestone","round_closed_outcome_and_host_candidate_hash","killed_close_carries_null_hash","builder_filed_report_reaches_the_log_with_task_id","report_task_id_stamped_from_dispatch_not_worker","report_task_contradiction_rejected","report_run_id_comes_from_the_round_directory","report_asserting_a_fake_run_id_is_still_attributed_to_its_directory"],"interfaces":"You are building the substrate every later slice reads. Four events, three readers.\n\n| event | payload you must provide | who reads it |\n|---|---|---|\n| `task.declared` | `taskId`, `milestoneId`, `spec` | populates a milestone's `required_task_ids` |\n| `round.dispatched` | `taskId`, `milestoneId` | the delivery fold \u2014 this is the run\u2192task binding |\n| `round.closed` | `outcome`, `candidateHash`, `files`, `taskId`, `milestoneId` | the delivery fold, and the fixture assembler |\n| `builder.reported` | `taskId`, added to the existing payload | the delivery fold |\n\n**`round.closed.files` is the most load-bearing field you produce.** It is a `path \u2192 digest` map,\nand the fixture assembler pulls each artifact out of the content-addressed store through it. Without\nit, nothing can be assembled and nothing can be judged.\n\n**`outcome` takes these values and no others:** `success` \u00b7 `failure` \u00b7 `killed` \u00b7 `timed_out` \u00b7\n`cancelled`. Readers branch on exactly these.\n\n**The task id is stamped by the host, from the dispatch record \u2014 never from the report body.** A\nreport naming a different task than the one it was dispatched against is an anomaly and counts as\nnothing. This applies to both identities: the run comes from the round directory, the task from the\ndispatch.\n\n**`candidateHash` is computed by the control host from broker evidence for the candidate artifacts\nat close time \u2014 never reported by the builder.** `killed` and `timed_out` carry\n`candidateHash: null`.\n\n**Do not add fields that nothing above reads.** If you believe you need one, you are outside this\nslice.","milestoneId":"5ad1deec-991b-469f-a83b-c6753476fb67","outcome":"A dispatched round is bound to a task, and every round ends with a record the host computed itself.\n\nWhen a builder reports done, the log carries a task identity nobody could have forged, and a frozen\nhash of what was actually produced.","points":null,"projectId":"bbae7d78-67ca-54c3-97ba-ef4cbfcec9db","scope":"**You may change:** `src/progressdesk/events.py` \u00b7 `src/progressdesk/loop.py` \u00b7\n`src/progressdesk/runtime.py` \u00b7 `src/progressdesk/desk.py`\n\n**You may not change:** anything under `src/progressdesk/acceptance/` \u00b7 `milestones.py` \u00b7\n`store.py` \u00b7 `report.py` \u00b7 any role brief.\n\n**Already correct in this repo \u2014 read it, use it, do not rewrite it:**\n\n- Reports are already per-round. `runtime.drain_reports()` and `runtime._round_dirs()` exist, and a\n  report is attributed to the round directory it was found in \u2014 never by what its body claims. **You\n  do not add a run id to anything.**\n- `_digests()` already turns bytes into `{name: \"sha256:...\"}` against the content-addressed\n  store, and `DispatchOutcome` already carries `.files`. You are hashing a map that exists. You are\n  not building collection or storage.\n- `DispatchOutcome.has_candidate` already means \"this round produced an artifact.\" Use it; do not\n  rename it.\n\n**Your decision:** the shape of the hash helper \u00b7 where the close is emitted in the dispatch flow \u00b7\nhelper names in the two files you edit.","taskId":"62c2691c-0fd8-4053-960a-09ce367900c1","title":"Build-loop prerequisites"}